CyberArk explicitly states that the GCP Account Management plugin supports account management with MFA for Google IAM user accounts. Change and Reconcile are performed through the linked GCP Service Account and ImpersonateUser, not by signing into the target Google account interactively.

https://docs.cyberark.com/privilege-cloud-standard/latest/en/content/pasimp/googlecloudplatform-account-management.htm


The MFA challenge belongs to an interactive sign-in of the target Google account. CPM does not perform that login. CyberArk uses the Admin SDK API to execute the password-management operation, and CyberArk specifically documents the Admin SDK as enabling administrative credentials to execute password-management APIs.
